-- a tree an asserted edge of which is retracted: the closure rows through it go, and every reader of them is the one a fresh
-- evaluation without the edge holds (a world answering the closure from its tree cannot say what a retraction left from
-- the witnesses of the rows, since it keeps none: it builds the tree again and reads again)
tree dtg_in(P, C) closure dtg_within.
dtg_in(a, b).
dtg_in(b, c).
dtg_in(c, d).
dtg_in(x, y).
dtg_hit(X) :- dtg_within(a, X).
dtg_pair(X, Y) :- dtg_within(X, Y), dtg_in(Y, _).
dtg_cnt(N) :- N is count(X, Y : dtg_within(X, Y)).
